Corresponding source
--------------------
The published files of a release are built from this repository at the
release's tag, v<version>, at https://github.com/trigcondition/sidecar-mods:
`make setup`, then `make release` for OS 1.73 and `make release OS=1.74` for
OS 1.74 (docs/ELEKLOADER.md), with the toolchain the release's TOOLCHAIN.txt
names (the bytes depend on the m68k-elf-as version). For OS 1.73 they are
rytm-sidecar-<version>.elemod and core-0.1.elemod; for OS 1.74
rytm-sidecar-<version>-os1.74.elemod and core-0.1-os1.74.elemod, each OS in
its own release folder. That tag holds the complete source of our bytes
(mods/, registry/, re/, tools/; the 1.74 addresses come from the 1.73 sources
through re/os/1.74.toml and tools/ostarget.py) and pins the exact third-party
sources the build uses (Makefile, tools/build.py, re/os/<os>.toml):

  - core-0.1.elemod (OS 1.73) is elekloader's core-ar2 0.1, built unchanged
    by elekloader's own builder from mods/core-ar2 and mods/core at
    elekloader commit 8972d70629f230af99c63c8624a886b33ec08299
    (https://github.com/irpina/elekloader, GPL-2.0-or-later);
  - core-0.1-os1.74.elemod (OS 1.74) is the same core-ar2 0.1 with
    upstream's own port to OS 1.74 (the "ports" block of its mod.json, by
    irpina and Iced-Cream), built unchanged by the same builder from
    mods/core-ar2 and mods/core at elekloader commit
    13fa795d601c52a7152c17554ae3b3f6f6ca8b05;
  - the builder, linker and packer are elekloader at commit
    c150ac583a4b7e6d64680d5592f4a40f409193f7.

Their source is also in each release folder, beside the files (GPL-2.0
section 3): for OS 1.73 elekloader-8972d70-core-ar2-src.tar.gz (mods/core and
mods/core-ar2 at 8972d70, with elekloader's LICENSE and NOTICE), for OS 1.74
elekloader-13fa795-core-ar2-src.tar.gz (the same at 13fa795), and in both
elekloader-c150ac5-src.tar.gz (all of elekloader at c150ac5).

Some of our stubs are generated from C (mods/*/build.sh says how); the C file
is the source, the generated stub.s is committed beside it.

Third-party code
----------------
Nothing below is copied into this repository. `make setup` fetches it into
vendor/ (git-ignored) at pinned commits, and the build executes it.

  vendor/elekloader
      https://github.com/irpina/elekloader, (C) 2026 irpina and contributors,
      GPL-2.0-or-later (its LICENSE and NOTICE; its js/ kit, not used here, is
      GPL-3.0-or-later). Builds the elemods, links them into the image
      with its core-ar2 (boot copier and hook bus), packs and checks the .syx.
      A built image, and core-0.1.elemod, contain elekloader's core-ar2 code.

  vendor/elektron-firmware-tool
      https://github.com/mischa85/elektron-firmware-tool, (C) 2026 Marcel
      Bierling, MIT licence (its LICENSE). Unpacks and repacks the .syx
      container; our checks extract every image with it.

